SUMMARY:Hope Café: Finding Connection
DESCRIPTION:Join us on two nights\, August 20th and September 25th\, to celebrate the start of fall with an evening at the International House Davis\, designed to build connection and community. Hope Café is a mix of a workshop and a party\, opening up a space where live music\, creative activities\, and guided conversations invite you to reflect and develop a new connection. \n  \nActivities include: community story sharing and playful creative exercises until 8:30 PM\, live world jazz by Nick Carvajal and Jim Frink\, and complimentary food and drinks provided by the Davis Food Co-Op. \n  \nTickets operate on a sliding scale of $15 – $25. Free tickets are available upon request by emailing office@internationalhousedavis.org. This event is open to community members ages 14 and older. \n  \nTo purchase tickets\, visit: https://secure.internationalhousedavis.org/nx/portal/neonevents/events?path=%2Fportal%2Fevents%2F49102
URL:https://hatefreetogether.org/event/hope-cafe-connection/2026-09-25/
LOCATION:International House Davis\, 10 College Park\, Davis\, 95616\, United States
CATEGORIES:Season of Connection
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/png:https://hatefreetogether.org/wp-content/uploads/Hope-Cafe-8.20.26-9.25.26-Website-1-e1786573900885.png
END:VEVENT
